  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Playing the Game",
    "section": "1.60",
    "heading": "The Order of Combat",
    "lineStart": 520,
    "lineEnd": 522
  },
  "section": "1.60",
  "rulesText": "A typical combat encounter is a clash between two sides: a flurry of weapon swings, feints, parries, footwork, and spellcasting. The game organizes combat into a cycle of rounds and turns. A round represents about 6 seconds in the game world. During a round, each participant in a battle takes a turn. The order of turns is determined at the beginning of combat when everyone rolls Initiative. Once everyone has taken a turn, the fight continues to the next round if neither side is defeated."
}
